Subject: In-place string accumulator

What this does
  In-place string accumulator.

Why we need it
  The register add duplicates both operands before calling the engine, so `JS_ConcatString2`'s in-place test can never fire and every `s += x` allocates a fresh rope.

What it adds
  `regvm_accum_append` (register-path port of the stack VM's `js_accum_append`) appends in place when `d == a` and the register provably holds the only reference to a normal non-atom string - the DRC state plus a scan of the register file and argument window for borrowed aliases; wired into threaded `T_BODY_RRR` / `regvm_t_binary_cpool` and monolith `REGVM_BIN_OP` / `L_ROP_binary_cpool`; step helpers regenerated to expose `rf->arg_buf`/`rf->argc`.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
